I still can't think of an elegant way to describe *that* to someone
else though.

Last night, some ideas that will (usually) speed things up came to me.

a) stop the AAAAA pass after the 2nd wiff or 1st gear turn.
b) fix two (or more) letters simultaneously

So, for the same tune (GFEDC):

1: AAAAA: wiff
2: BBBBB: wiff
3: DCCCC: 1 turn, 1 tumbler (xxxxx)
4: ADCCC: 1 turn, 1 tumbler (xxxxx)
5: AADCC: 1 turn, 1 tumbler (xxxDC or xxxCD)
6: FEEDC: 3 turns, 1 tumbler (GxxDC)
7: GFEDC: 5 turns, solved.

I'll have to flesh it out some more for duplicate letters, the
